# MiMi-d for WebCLAP

MiMi-d (a polyphonic synthesizer by Ricard Wanderlof (polluxsynth)), ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official release.

- MiMi-d: https://github.com/polluxsynth/audio-plugins (commit 34131ce, GPL-2.0)
- [DPF](https://github.com/DISTRHO/DPF) (commit 4238e1c), the DISTRHO Plugin Framework the plugin is written with
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-mimid.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 2** (`LICENSE`).

MiMi-d is under the GNU General Public License, version 2, as stated in the repository's `LICENSE` and the sources' headers (`licenses/MiMi-d-GPL-2.0.txt`). Its engine contains code from OB-Xd, copyright 2013-2014 Filatov Vadim, which stays under its own copyright notices in the sources. DPF is ISC (`licenses/DPF-ISC.txt`), which is compatible with the GPL; `module.wasm` as a whole is distributed under the GPL.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

The bundle holds the DSP only (`module.wasm`): DPF's own CLAP wrapper compiled to WebAssembly. The plugin's graphical
editor is not part of it, hosts show the plugin's parameters instead.

## Components

| Component | Copyright | License |
|---|---|---|
| [MiMi-d](https://github.com/polluxsynth/audio-plugins) incl. the `plugins/mimid` engine | 2023-2025 Ricard Wanderlof | GPL-2.0 (`licenses/MiMi-d-GPL-2.0.txt`) |
| OB-Xd code inside MiMi-d's engine | 2013-2014 Filatov Vadim | as stated in the source headers |
| [DPF](https://github.com/DISTRHO/DPF), incl. its CLAP wrapper | 2012-2025 Filipe Coelho | ISC (`licenses/DPF-ISC.txt`) |
| [CLAP](https://github.com/free-audio/clap) headers, bundled with DPF | 2021 Alexandre Bique | MIT |
| WebCLAP kit ([open-webclap](https://github.com/andremichelle/open-webclap) `modules/juce_webclap/juce_webclap_standalone.cpp`) | André Michelle | MIT |
| WebCLAP port ([open-webclap](https://github.com/andremichelle/open-webclap) `ports/mimid`, `ports/dpf`) | open-webclap contributors | MIT |
| Emscripten sysroot, linked statically: musl libc, LLVM libc++ and libc++abi | musl authors; LLVM Project | MIT; Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions |

